{
  "provenance": {
    "source": "Structural-trajectory region concordance v3: country-level development archetypes (World Bank income classification, FY2025) aggregated to EXIOBASE coarse-v3 blocks with PER-DRIVER, TIME-VARYING weights — population shares (UN WPP 2024, per knot) and output shares (PWT 10.01 rgdpo 2019); v2's static IMF-2024 GDP weights are retained as the participation proxy and back-compat block_membership.",
    "source_version": "structural-concordance-v3",
    "licence": "derived mapping (CC BY 4.0); World Bank income classification (CC BY 4.0), IMF WEO (public, cited not redistributed)",
    "reference_year": 2024,
    "world_bank_vintage": "FY2025 (July 2024 release; Russia = high-income in this vintage)",
    "retrieved": "2026-09-16",
    "notes": "Fixes review P1 (2026-08-29): the coarse-v3 blocks RoW_Asia / RoW_America / RoW_Europe mix income levels, so a SINGLE archetype cannot be derived from an income rule. This artifact instead assigns each MEMBER COUNTRY an archetype (N=high-income proxy, S=low/middle-income proxy) by the World Bank FY2025 income classification, and aggregates each block's trajectory as the GDP-WEIGHTED blend of its members' archetype paths — so a mixed block (e.g. RoW_Asia, which contains high-income AU/KR/TW and emerging ID plus the WA rest-of-Asia aggregate) gets a blended, not a wholly-emerging, path. The World Bank vintage is pinned explicitly (FY2025), which places Russia in the HIGH-income group — resolving the earlier RU ambiguity. GDP weights are IMF WEO Oct-2024 nominal GDP shares (current USD), documented and reviewable; the W* rest-of-region aggregates carry the block's residual weight tagged as an emerging-economy proxy. The archetype rate paths themselves live in trajectories_v1.json (N/S). This file is the reviewable bridge; the loader aggregates with these weights.",
    "gdp_weight_note": "Weights are approximate 2024 nominal-GDP shares within each block (IMF WEO Oct-2024), rounded to 3 dp and renormalised to sum to 1 per block. They are documented illustrative weights, not a committed extraction pipeline (a reproducible IMF/WB extraction is a follow-up, consistent with the trajectories_v1 reproducibility caveat).",
    "v3_note": "v3 (review-9 1c 2026-09-16): adds PER-DRIVER, TIME-VARYING block_weights. population weights = UN WPP 2024 per-country population at each knot (2025/2035/2050 — genuinely year-varying); output weights = PWT 10.01 rgdpo (2019, held flat). driver_weight_class maps population→population, productivity→output, labour_participation→the static v2 block_membership GDP weights (no per-country labour-force series available — documented proxy). The EXIOBASE rest-of-region aggregates (W*) have no single ISO3 and retain their v2 residual share, with named members renormalised around it. v2 block_membership is preserved for back-compat."
  },
